flowchart TB
    accTitle: The live facts of the home pages
    accDescr: Every two hours the Dashboard workflow of the blueprint publishes repos.json, history.json and releases.atom at dennis-otto.github.io/repo-blueprint/dashboard/. Every day, and with every change of main, the Docs workflow builds this website, and its hooks write the repository of every project and the level of its OpenSSF Best Practices, which they read from bestpractices.dev, into its card. As a home page loads in a reader's browser, docs/javascripts/projects.js reads repos.json from the same address, or history.json when it can't, and writes the release, its day and the quality numbers into every card and the newest release of each project under What's new. Without the data or the script, every card keeps what the build wrote. A feed reader follows releases.atom, which What's new links.

    dashboard(["The Dashboard workflow<br>of the blueprint<br>every two hours"])
    data["/repo-blueprint/dashboard/<br>repos.json<br>history.json<br>releases.atom"]
    build(["The Docs workflow<br>every day and with<br>every change of main"])
    levels["bestpractices.dev<br>the level of<br>every project"]
    hooks["The hooks of the website<br>every card with its<br>repository and its level"]
    page["A home page in a reader's browser"]
    script["projects.js<br>on the same origin"]
    cards["Every card<br>the release, its day<br>and the quality numbers"]
    news["What's new<br>the newest release<br>of each project"]
    still["No data or no script<br>the card keeps<br>what the build wrote"]
    reader(["A feed reader"])

    dashboard --> data
    build --> hooks
    levels --> hooks
    hooks --> page --> script
    data --> script
    script --> cards & news
    script -. "no data" .-> still
    news -- "links releases.atom" --> reader

